# Cross-DC firewall change request (template) — ingress replication path

**Purpose:** Paste into a network-team change ticket before cutover when using a **dedicated ingress shard** on the replication VLAN (Path B in the [architecture overview](../../messaging/kafka/cross-dc-architecture-overview.md)).

**Contrast:** Multus path uses [firewall-change-request.md.example](firewall-change-request.md.example) (TCP 9095, pod IP pools).

---

## Summary

Allow **bidirectional** replication VLAN traffic between datacenters for Kafka Cluster Linking over a **dedicated OpenShift IngressController** on TCP **443** (TLS passthrough to brokers).

Traffic terminates at **router frontend addresses** on the replication subnet — not broker pod IPs directly.

## Datacenters

| DC | Replication subnet | Ingress frontend (${frontend_mode}) |
|---|---|---|
| ${dc_a_id} | ${dc_a_subnet} | ${dc_a_frontend_targets} |
| ${dc_b_id} | ${dc_b_subnet} | ${dc_b_frontend_targets} |

`${frontend_mode}`: `vip` (single IP per DC) or `dns_lb` (multiple router node repl IPs).

## Required flows

| Direction | Source | Destination | Protocol | Port | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| ${dc_a_id} → ${dc_b_id} | ${dc_a_subnet} | ${dc_b_frontend_targets} | TCP | 443 | SNI to broker Route hostnames |
| ${dc_b_id} → ${dc_a_id} | ${dc_b_subnet} | ${dc_a_frontend_targets} | TCP | 443 | reverse direction |
| Both | replication subnets | replication subnets | ICMP | — | path MTU troubleshooting (optional) |

**Long-lived TCP:** Cluster Linking requires persistent connections — avoid aggressive idle timeouts on firewalls/load balancers on this path.

## MTU

Expected end-to-end MTU on VLAN 200: **${expected_mtu}** bytes.

## Explicit non-goals

- No default route on the replication VLAN interface (host or pod).
- No requirement to reach cluster API or internet over this VLAN.
- This ticket is **not** for the default `apps.*` ingress VIP on the machine network.

## Verification contact

Platform team verifies: DNS resolves replication hostnames to repl-subnet targets; `openssl s_client` to broker Route hostname on :443 from remote DC. See [ingress verification checklist](../../messaging/kafka/cross-dc-ingress-alternative.md#verification-checklist-ingress-path).
